# Settings of the HTTPS proxy (ADR 0030, `docker compose --profile tls up -d`). Copy to
# proxy.env. Only the proxy reads this file; it holds no secrets.
# Needs DNS for TLS_DOMAIN pointing at this host and ports 80 and 443 open.
TLS_DOMAIN=afspraak.example.nl
# Receives notices from the CA (account, policy changes).
ACME_EMAIL=<operations mailbox>
# Default Let's Encrypt production. Trial runs:
# ACME_CA=https://acme-staging-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory
# Own certificate instead of ACME (ADR 0064): put the PEM chain and the key in ./certs, readable
# by uid 10001, and name them here; the proxy then manages nothing and renewal is yours.
# Restart the proxy after replacing the files.
# TLS_CERT_FILE=/certs/fullchain.pem
# TLS_KEY_FILE=/certs/privkey.pem
# The superuser may instead upload a certificate in the portal (ADR 0070); the proxy picks it
# up within this many seconds (2-300). Files named above win over the portal's choice.
# TLS_PORTAL_POLL_SECONDS=10
